                <content>
                  <p>6  Application provision—validity of visa applications</p>
                </content>
                <subsection eId="schedule-2__amdact-1__item-5__qstr-1__subsec-1">
                  <num>1</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>(1)	The repeal of subparagraph 46(1)(e)(vi) and Subdivision AK of <ref href="#dvs-3">Division 3</ref> of Part 2 of the <i>Migration Act 1958</i> by this Schedule applies in relation to the following:</p>
                  </content>
                  <paragraph eId="schedule-2__amdact-1__item-5__qstr-1__subsec-1__para-a">
                    <num>a</num>
                    <content>
                      <p>an application for a visa made on or after the commencement of this item;</p>
                    </content>
                  </paragraph>
                  <paragraph eId="schedule-2__amdact-1__item-5__qstr-1__subsec-1__para-b">
                    <num>b</num>
                    <content>
                      <p>an application for a visa made before the commencement of this item if, immediately before that commencement, a decision has not been made that the application is not a valid application.</p>
                    </content>
                  </paragraph>
                </subsection>
                <subsection eId="schedule-2__amdact-1__item-5__qstr-1__subsec-2">
                  <num>2</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>(2)	For an application of a kind mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) of this item, subparagraph 46(1)(e)(vi) and Subdivision AK of <ref href="#dvs-3">Division 3</ref> of Part 2 of the <i>Migration Act 1958</i> are to be taken to have been repealed immediately before the application was made.</p>
                  </content>
